> Good morning,

I tried several other things, and I was able to fix my problem.

What I did not know is that the following actually works:

u= "Gout =~   A.le.gout.caractéristique.d.un.emmental + A.un.gout.complexe + A.le.gout.d.un.emmental.qui.a.eu.le.temps.de <http://a.le.gout.d.un.emmental.qui.a.eu.le.temps.de/>  \n   Texture   =~   Colle.en.bouche + A.une.texture.granuleuse..friable  + A.une.texture.caoutchouteuse  \n   Noteglobale   =~   Note.globale    \n    Noteglobale ~ Gout     \n      Noteglobale ~ Texture     "

The sem() function reads that as if it was written in multiple lines, and doesn't just read \n as if it was text like the print() function for example.
Thus, changing my code to add \n where needed fixed my problem.

Regards,

Joël

