> Could you please show me if I should stop inspect the invariance across groups. If not, what should I do to test measurement invariance of this scale?

Sounds like you should read some literature on testing invariance, in particular on partial invariance (e.g., http://dx.doi.org/10.3758/s13428-013-0430-2).  You can post general questions (i.e., not software-specific) on SEMNET <http://www2.gsu.edu/~mkteer/semnet.html>, which is a much larger forum of SEM experts.  Once you know what method you need to use, you might find the partialInvariance() function in the semTools package useful.

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
