> with FUN = coef, I can extract all parameters of interest (e.g. a1 & b1), but I won't get the parameterEstimates of my indriect effect (i.e., a1b1) as well as my total effect -> how can I extract coef and my bootstrapped CI of the indirect effect?

See my original response :-)  You can create any user-defined parameters in the bootstrapLavaan() output by using the same definitions you used in the model syntax.  (It is probably easier if you save the bootstrapLavaan() output as a data.frame first, then add the user-defined parameters as new variables.)

> out <- as.data.frame(bootstrapLavaan(..., FUN = coef))
> out$ab <- out$a * out*b
> quantile(out$ab, probs = c(.025, .975))

Note that if you want a bias-corrected, accelerated CI, you can define a function that accepts your data frame and an arbitrary index variable to extract rows in a bootstrap sample, then fits the model and returns the coefficients, including (or only returning) the indirect effect.  Then you could use the boot() function directly (from the boot package), enabling you to extract the BCa CI using the boot.ci <http://boot.ci>() function.

